{% use '@Altcha/fields.html.twig' %}

{#
    The captcha widget is a custom element that keeps the solved proof of work in a DOM of its own, and the bundle
    gives it a fresh random id on every render, which makes the `data-live-ignore` the bundle puts on it
    ineffective: the live component re-renders on every field change (`data-model="on(change)|*"`), and the morph
    replaces the contents of an element whose id differs from the rendered one before it reads that attribute. The
    widget was therefore emptied by the first change to another field, leaving nothing to solve and a sign-up that
    could not be submitted.

    A container with an id that does not change between renders is what the morph reads instead, so it skips the
    container and everything in it, including the input the widget writes its payload into. The row's errors are
    rendered outside this block and still re-render.
#}
{% block altcha_widget %}
    <div id="{{ id }}_altcha" data-live-ignore>
        {{ parent() }}
    </div>
{% endblock %}
